    "engine": "jupyter",
    "markdown": "---\ngd-head-tags:\n  - >-\n    `<script type=\"application/ld+json\">[{\"@context\": \"https://schema.org\",\n    \"@type\": \"SoftwareSourceCode\", \"name\": \"Edgecase\", \"description\":\n    \"High-performance graph analysis library\", \"codeRepository\":\n    \"https://github.com/rich-iannone/edgecase\", \"license\":\n    \"https://opensource.org/licenses/MIT\", \"url\":\n    \"https://rich-iannone.github.io/edgecase\", \"documentation\":\n    \"https://rich-iannone.github.io/edgecase\", \"programmingLanguage\": {\"@type\":\n    \"ComputerLanguage\", \"name\": \"Python\"}}, {\"@context\": \"https://schema.org\",\n    \"@type\": \"WebPage\", \"name\": \"Graph.layout_arf - Edgecase\", \"isPartOf\":\n    {\"@type\": \"WebSite\", \"name\": \"Edgecase\"}, \"url\":\n    \"https://rich-iannone.github.io/edgecase/reference/Graph.layout_arf.html\"}]</script>`{=html}\nopen-graph:\n  title: >-\n    [Graph.layout_arf()]{.doc-object-name .doc-function .doc-label\n    .doc-label-method} | Edgecase\n  description: >-\n    Place the nodes with the attractive and repulsive forces (ARF) layout.\ntwitter-card:\n  title: >-\n    [Graph.layout_arf()]{.doc-object-name .doc-function .doc-label\n    .doc-label-method} | Edgecase\n  description: >-\n    Place the nodes with the attractive and repulsive forces (ARF) layout.\ntitle: >-\n  [Graph.layout_arf()]{.doc-object-name .doc-function .doc-label\n  .doc-label-method}\nbody-classes: doc-api-page doc-py-api-page\nshift-heading-level-by: 0\nbread-crumbs: false\ntoc-depth: 3\ndescription-meta: >-\n  Place the nodes with the attractive and repulsive forces (ARF) layout.\npage-navigation: false\nhtml-table-processing: none\n---\n\n::: {.doc-subject}\n\nPlace the nodes with the attractive and repulsive forces (ARF) layout.\n:::\n\n::: {.doc-usage-source}\nUsage\n\n[Source](https://github.com/rich-iannone/edgecase/blob/main/python/edgecase/graph.py#L6207-L6321){target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"}\n:::\n\n::: {.doc-signature .doc-function}\n```pythonsignature\nGraph.layout_arf(\n    scaling=1.0,\n    a=1.1,\n    etol=1e-06,\n    dt=0.001,\n    max_iter=1000,\n    initial=None,\n    scale=1.0,\n    center=(0.0, 0.0),\n    seed=None,\n    attr_name=None,\n    return_dict=False,\n)\n```\n:::\n\n::: {.doc-text}\n\n![ARF layout](/assets/graphs/layout-arf.light.svg){.lightbox fig-alt=\"On the left, a barbell graph scattered at random: two triangles, nodes 1 to 3 and 5 to 7, joined through node 4. On the right, layout_arf(seed=19) pulls joined nodes together and pushes every pair apart, so the two triangles sit apart with node 4 bridging them.\" width=\"100%\"}\n\nARF (Geipel, 2007) joins every pair of nodes by a weak spring of strength `1`,\nstrengthened to `a=` for adjacent pairs, and lets every pair repel with force\n`rho / d`, where `rho = scaling * sqrt(n)`. The springs on all pairs hold the layout\ntogether in a round, evenly filled disc, avoiding the large gaps a spring layout can\nleave, while the stronger springs on edges pull connected groups together.\nPositions follow the force field in small time steps `dt=` until the summed force\nfalls to `etol=` or `max_iter=` steps have run. The result is centered and scaled so\nthe largest coordinate is `scale=`.\n\nThis follows NetworkX's `arf_layout()` with two differences: edges strengthen the\nspring between their ends in both directions (NetworkX strengthens only the\n`source -> target` entry of the spring matrix, so directed graphs get lopsided\nforces), and the result is rescaled (NetworkX returns raw coordinates). Each step\ncosts `O(n^2)`. Edge weights are not used.\n\nPositions are stored as `[x, y]` lists in the `attr_name=` node attribute; see\n`layout_circular()`.\n:::\n\n## Parameters {.doc-parameters}\n\n::: {.doc-definition-items}\n<code>[scaling]{.doc-parameter-name}[:]{.doc-parameter-annotation-sep} [float]{.doc-parameter-annotation} [=]{.doc-parameter-default-sep .op} [[1.0]{.fl}]{.doc-parameter-default}</code>\n\n:   Strength of the repulsion, which sets the size of the disc. Default is `1.0`.\n\n<code>[a]{.doc-parameter-name}[:]{.doc-parameter-annotation-sep} [float]{.doc-parameter-annotation} [=]{.doc-parameter-default-sep .op} [[1.1]{.fl}]{.doc-parameter-default}</code>\n\n:   Spring strength between adjacent nodes; must be greater than `1`. Larger values\n    separate clusters more clearly. Default is `1.1`.\n\n<code>[etol]{.doc-parameter-name}[:]{.doc-parameter-annotation-sep} [float]{.doc-parameter-annotation} [=]{.doc-parameter-default-sep .op} [[1e-06]{.fl}]{.doc-parameter-default}</code>\n\n:   Stop once the summed force on all nodes falls to this. Default is `1e-6`.\n\n<code>[dt]{.doc-parameter-name}[:]{.doc-parameter-annotation-sep} [float]{.doc-parameter-annotation} [=]{.doc-parameter-default-sep .op} [[0.001]{.fl}]{.doc-parameter-default}</code>\n\n:   Time step of the simulation. Default is `1e-3`.\n\n<code>[max_iter]{.doc-parameter-name}[:]{.doc-parameter-annotation-sep} [int]{.doc-parameter-annotation} [=]{.doc-parameter-default-sep .op} [[1000]{.dv}]{.doc-parameter-default}</code>\n\n:   Maximum number of steps. Default is `1000`.\n\n<code>[initial]{.doc-parameter-name}[:]{.doc-parameter-annotation-sep} [Optional[Union[str, dict]]]{.doc-parameter-annotation} [=]{.doc-parameter-default-sep .op} [None]{.doc-parameter-default}</code>\n\n:   Starting positions, as the name of a node attribute holding `(x, y)` pairs or a\n    dict mapping node IDs or labels to pairs. Nodes without one start at random. If\n    `None` (default), all nodes start at random in the unit square.\n\n<code>[scale]{.doc-parameter-name}[:]{.doc-parameter-annotation-sep} [Optional[float]]{.doc-parameter-annotation} [=]{.doc-parameter-default-sep .op} [[1.0]{.fl}]{.doc-parameter-default}</code>\n\n:   Largest coordinate after rescaling. `None` keeps the raw coordinates (`center=` is\n    then ignored). Default is `1.0`.\n\n<code>[center]{.doc-parameter-name}[:]{.doc-parameter-annotation-sep} [tuple[float, float]]{.doc-parameter-annotation} [=]{.doc-parameter-default-sep .op} [(0.0, 0.0)]{.doc-parameter-default}</code>\n\n:   Center of the layout, as `(x, y)`. Default is the origin.\n\n<code>[seed]{.doc-parameter-name}[:]{.doc-parameter-annotation-sep} [Optional[int]]{.doc-parameter-annotation} [=]{.doc-parameter-default-sep .op} [None]{.doc-parameter-default}</code>\n\n:   Integer seed for the random starting positions. If `None` (default), the layout\n    differs on every call.\n\n<code>[attr_name]{.doc-parameter-name}[:]{.doc-parameter-annotation-sep} [Optional[str]]{.doc-parameter-annotation} [=]{.doc-parameter-default-sep .op} [None]{.doc-parameter-default}</code>\n\n:   Node attribute to store the positions in. If `None` (default), uses `\"pos\"`.\n\n<code>[return_dict]{.doc-parameter-name}[:]{.doc-parameter-annotation-sep} [bool]{.doc-parameter-annotation} [=]{.doc-parameter-default-sep .op} [[False]{.va}]{.doc-parameter-default}</code>\n\n:   If `True`, returns a dictionary instead of self. If `False` (default), stores the\n    positions on the nodes and returns self for chaining.\n:::\n\n## Returns {.doc-returns}\n\n::: {.doc-definition-items}\n<code> [Union[dict[int, tuple[float, float]], Graph]]{.doc-parameter-annotation}</code>\n\n:   If `return_dict=` is `True`: dictionary mapping node IDs to `(x, y)` tuples. If\n    `return_dict=` is `False` (default): returns self for method chaining.\n:::\n\n## Raises {.doc-raises}\n\n::: {.doc-definition-items}\n<code> [ValueError]{.doc-parameter-annotation}</code>\n\n:   If `a=` is not greater than `1`, `scaling=` or `dt=` is not positive, `etol=` is\n    negative, an initial position is not a pair of finite numbers, or `scale=` or\n    `center=` is invalid.\n:::\n\n## Examples {.doc-examples}\n\nTwo cliques joined by a path, with a large `a=` to keep the cliques tight:\n\n::: {#d2518cfd .cell execution_count=1}\n``` {.python .cell-code}\nimport edgecase as ec\n\nec.Graph().add_barbell_graph(6, 3).layout_arf(a=3, seed=5).plot(layout=\"pos\")\n```\n\n::: {.cell-output .cell-output-display execution_count=1}\n```{=html}\n<div style=\"position:relative;display:inline-block\">\n<svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"600\" height=\"400\" viewBox=\"109.3 14.0 381.4 392.0\" style=\"font-family: -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, 'Segoe UI', Roboto, 'Helvetica Neue', Arial, sans-serif;\">\n<rect x=\"109.3\" y=\"14.0\" width=\"381.4\" height=\"392.0\" fill=\"#fafafa\"/>\n<path d=\"M164.2,212.5 C166.5,215.9 170.9,229.0 177.8,232.6 C184.7,236.1 201.1,233.6 205.7,233.8\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#94a3b8\" stroke-width=\"2.1\" stroke-opacity=\"0.4\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" data-edge=\"11-10-0\" data-attrs='{}'/>\n<path d=\"M169.3,191.5 C172.3,189.8 182.0,186.7 187.5,181.4 C193.0,176.1 199.8,163.2 202.2,159.6\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#94a3b8\" stroke-width=\"2.1\" stroke-opacity=\"0.4\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" data-edge=\"11-12-1\" data-attrs='{}'/>\n<line x1=\"169.8\" y1=\"205.9\" x2=\"173.0\" y2=\"207.4\" stroke=\"#94a3b8\" stroke-width=\"2.1\" stroke-opacity=\"0.4\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" data-edge=\"11-13-2\" data-attrs='{}'/>\n<line x1=\"162.9\" y1=\"185.1\" x2=\"165.5\" y2=\"180.2\" stroke=\"#94a3b8\" stroke-width=\"2.1\" stroke-opacity=\"0.4\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" data-edge=\"11-14-3\" data-attrs='{}'/>\n<path d=\"M154.3,183.3 C154.0,179.5 151.0,167.4 152.8,160.6 C154.6,153.8 163.2,145.6 165.3,142.6\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#94a3b8\" stroke-width=\"2.1\" stroke-opacity=\"0.4\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" data-edge=\"11-15-4\" data-attrs='{}'/>\n<line x1=\"389.1\" y1=\"111.7\" x2=\"380.8\" y2=\"104.3\" stroke=\"#94a3b8\" stroke-width=\"2.1\" stroke-opacity=\"0.4\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" data-edge=\"3-1-5\" data-attrs='{}'/>\n<line x1=\"408.8\" y1=\"108.6\" x2=\"417.2\" y2=\"93.9\" stroke=\"#94a3b8\" stroke-width=\"2.1\" stroke-opacity=\"0.4\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" data-edge=\"3-2-6\" data-attrs='{}'/>\n<line x1=\"416.9\" y1=\"122.6\" x2=\"428.7\" y2=\"122.7\" 